WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.680
(Thud, beast roars) HUH! WHAT THE FUCK! HI?! I'M NOT IN MY SHIP! OOOOOH!

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.640
Hello everybody. My name is Markiplier and welcome back to Subnautica.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:18.460
Now, by some amazing stroke of luck, with the official full release of this game, my save game file still works.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.100
Which means, that I am in a great position

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.300
In the middle of the ocean, surrounded by nothing, but death and only (laughs) darkness awaits me!

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.220
But, this is the full release of the game.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.240
This is what I've been waiting for. This is what we've all been waiting for because now...

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.140
We can get the hell off of this damn ocean planet!

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.660
(Maniacal laughter)

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.900
Number one: I need to get back to my shit, which is way over there. Big Box Berry is in the ocean-

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:46.940
What is that?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.680
Well, I have a new message

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.080
I'm sure this is gonna be good!

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.100
Hello?

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:57.840
Robotic voice: This is an automated distress signal from Lifepod 12, co-ordinates attached.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:06.760
Robotic Voice: Warning: Lifepod has sunk beyond safe diving distance. Do not attempt retrieval without submersible support.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.500
Automated female voice: Signal location uploaded to PDA.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.440
Okay? Alright, then. Well!

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.240
That sucks for them!

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.300
They can suck a big ol' donger because I ain't gonna come their way

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.540
...And I'm pretty sure they're dead no matter what happens.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.820
Now, where we are I'm not 100% sure. But Bubblebutt is right there.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.160
Which means that we have a mode of transportation and things don't look so dire, but number one I gotta say

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.920
Before I start anything, I'm really happy that this game is fully released.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.420
I was tempted to start over, all over again

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.180
I really was

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:36.900
To play from the beginning

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.460
But I've already done that and I've come so far in this one

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:46.500
And I've taken so much time and patience to be able to do this, that I've kind of gotten to this point where

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.960
I'm in love with the game. I really am. I hate the ocean! Oh, don't get me wrong!

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.340
I hate the ocean and we're gonna have to explore a lot of stuff that we've seen already anyway

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.280
And I'm gonna set out some objectives that we got to do, but it is good to be back

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:07.100
It is really really good to be back. It's good to see this game finally released. They've done tons of optimizations to the game

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:13.880
They've made it polished. They've actually fully released it with the storyline all intact. Everything on the Aurora that is able to be gotten

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.900
is available over there, which means that

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.760
Number one: I'm gonna go back to the Aurora.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.980
Number two: I'm gonna retrieve all my shit.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.760
Number three: I'm gonna start farming up materials.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:26.680
And number four: We are gonna launchie the hellie out of here

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.940
(mumbling) Where's this...

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:33.680
Here! We are gonna launchie the hellie out of here. We've got our mobile vehicle bay over with, uh,

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.660
Jeffrey, Billy, Samwise, and Marshall! I remembered those off of the top my head

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.740
I didn't even need to look 'em up!

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.340
Jeffrey Billy, Samwise and Marshall...

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.900
They're over there by the ship.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.040
In our first base that we built in the shadow of the Aurora.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.360
So what I'm gonna do right now, is I'm gonna retrieve everything that we have

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.820
I'm gonna go back to the Sea Emperor's... place.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.340
because apparently, uh

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.760
I, uh, I'm not cured.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.440
If I take off this glove here... Lemme show you something.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.120
It's horrible, but uh, let me self-scan, I guess.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:02:59.880
Uh-oh.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.300
Yep, I'm infected! Which, if I recall, I was not that way before!

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.580
I'm not 100 percent sure...

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.840
But I don't remember exactly where we left off, and I wasn't bothered to be checked so

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.600
(Screams)

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.900
Maybe we can hit that on the way back.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.100
Woah!

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.900
Hey, an animation! We got a temperature re--

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.300
--Why do we have a temperature reading? Is there some dynamic where--

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.300
Uh-oh. It's getting night.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.760
Oh shit that went quick...wai--Whoa whoa whoa whoa oh?

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.680
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh my god. That is so cool.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.720
Holy shit.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.220
I mean, I think I know it did that before, but it didn't do that so dramatically.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.320
That is an eclipse of the goddamn everything.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.120
Oh my goodness gravy!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.280
Uhehhhahay

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:45.960
Hey, hang on, let me stand on my Bubblebutt.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.200
Aww, that is so PRETTY!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.840
We got stuff to do. Number one, first and foremost we got to take care of this disease

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.800
